# GPT-6.1 Sol — findings by Claude Fable 5.1

- Source: OpenAI/GPT-6.1 Sol, e.g. OpenAI (`gpt-6.1-sol`)
- Date: 2026-10-09 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`
## Model card
- **Name:** GPT-6.1 Sol (paid; no Free-tier wording found on any host)
- **Short description:** OpenAI's mid-tier GPT-6.1-family model, an upgrade to GPT-6 Sol positioned as "near-Astra intelligence" for agentic coding, computer use and professional/document work at one-fifth of GPT-6 Astra's token prices. Variant note: sibling of GPT-6 Astra (flagship) / GPT-6 Luna (small); a separate "Ultrafast" serving tier (~300 tok/s per VentureBeat) was reported — not verified as a distinct model ID.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI API (ID `gpt-6.1-sol`, per Azure AI Foundry catalog slug and OpenRouter `openai/gpt-6.1-sol`); Microsoft Azure AI Foundry (`gpt-6.1-sol`); OpenRouter (`openai/gpt-6.1-sol`); OpenCode Zen — availability confirmed by OpenCode's announcement (x.com/opencode, 2026-09-29) and a models.dev PR (#8401, "Fix Zen GPT-6.1 Sol cached-read pricing"); the exact Zen ID string was not verified (pi.dev slug is `opencode/gpt-6-1-sol`). Responses vs Chat Completions API support: no verified public statement found.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-09-29 (OpenAI system-card addendum dated 2026-09-29; TechCrunch 2026-09-29); knowledge cutoff: no verified public value found.
- **IDs:** `openai/gpt-6.1-sol` (OpenRouter); `gpt-6.1-sol` (Azure). No Free ID exists on Zen (none found); paid Zen listing exists but exact ID string not verified.
- **Context window:** no verified public value found (not retrieved from official docs before tool limit).
- **Modalities:** text in/out verified; reasoning: yes (official post references "low/medium/maximum reasoning effort" settings); PDF/document handling evidenced via GDP.pdf eval (official); image/audio/video input, tool-call and JSON-mode support: no verified public spec retrieved.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-09):** Cached input **$0.10/1M** (official OpenAI post; stated as 95% below standard input and 50% below GPT-6 Sol's cached price). Standard input therefore implied ≈$2.00/1M, and official post states Sol is one-fifth of Astra's $10.00/$50.00 — but standard in/out figures for Sol itself were not directly displayed in retrieved text, so treat $2.00/$10.00 as derived, not verified. Paid only; no free-tier privacy caveat applies.
- **Architecture:** proprietary, closed weights; parameter count/MoE not disclosed. System card: Preparedness Framework rating "Critical" for cybersecurity and "High" for biological/chemical; uses the same safeguards stack as GPT-6 Astra.
